<title>USA: Citicorp vice chairman retires.</title>
<headline>Citicorp vice chairman retires.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citicorp said on Tuesday that Pei-yuan Chia retired as vice chairman and director, effective at the end of August.</p>
<p>Citicorp's board now consists of 13 members, the company said.</p>
<p>Chia announced plans to retire in January after a career with the company that began in 1974 and led to his appointment as vice chairman in January 1994, Citicorp said.</p>
<p>Chia has headed the consumer banking business at Citicorp, the company said in January.</p>
</text>
